## Workspaces

Select **Workspace** in the side bar. A workspace is where a team's work is organised. There are two kinds:

- **Suite workspaces**, one for each suite your firm uses — for example **Secretary**, **Tax** and **CRM**. Each has its AI employee. You can open a suite workspace if your administrator has granted the suite to you or to your department; tenant admins can open all of them. Otherwise the page says **Access denied: this suite requires an explicit grant or a tenant admin role.**
- **Workspaces your firm creates**, either a **Cross-department workspace** or a **Department workspace**.

To change workspace, select the workspace name at the top of the workspace side bar and choose from the list.

The workspace side bar can contain:

| Entry | Use |
|---|---|
| **Triage** | Notes waiting to be sorted. |
| **My Week** | Your work for the week. |
| **Cases** | The case board (below). Shown in the Secretary and Tax workspaces and in workspaces that have case types. **Templates** under it holds the case templates; see [Case templates](/en/case-templates/before-you-start/). |
| Boards | Table-style boards for the team's own lists. A **Main** board is visible to everyone in the workspace; a **Private** board only to its creator and the people they invite. Managers create boards and folders with **+**. |
| **Favorites** | Boards you marked as favourites. |
| **My agents** | Opens a chat with the workspace's AI employee. |

The CRM workspace has **Opportunity**, **Dashboard** and **Services & Packages** instead of cases; see [CRM · Contracts](/en/crm/overview/).

## Find a case

Select **Cases**. The board shows each case as a card in a column for its status:

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **Ready to start** | Created, work not started. |
| **Prep** | Being prepared. |
| **Review** | Being reviewed. |
| **Waiting for client** | Waiting for the client — documents, answers or signatures. |
| **Ready to file** | Ready to be filed with the authority. |
| **Done** | Completed. |
| **Blocked** | Cannot continue until something is resolved. |

Use **Search cases**, **Person** and **Filter** to narrow the board. Under **View settings**, choose **Kanban** or **List**. To keep a set of filters, use **Views** › **Save view**.

Select a card to open the case. The **⋯** menu of a card has **Reassign…**, **Cancel case…** and **Reopen case**.

## Start a case

{% steps %}
1. On the **Cases** board, select **+ New Case**.
2. Choose the **Case type** and the **Client**. **Assigned to**, **Case title**, **Tags**, **Start**, **Due** and **Description** are optional; a case without a title is named automatically.
3. Select **Create Case**.
4. Under **Role assignment**, assign the people for each role of the case with **Assign now**, or choose **Do this later**.
{% /steps %}

The dialog shows how many credits the case uses, and for how many days it can be cancelled free of charge.

The same dialog also opens from a company: on the company's **Cases** tab, select **Start a Case**; the client is then filled in.

{% aside type="note" title="Who can start a case" %}
Tenant admins, managers of the department that owns the case type, and partners can start cases. If **+ New Case** cannot be selected, point at it to see why, or ask your manager.
{% /aside %}

## The case page

The top of a case shows its name and client, and an information strip with **Client**, **Assigned to**, **Status**, **Due** and the progress of its **Tasks**. A bookkeeping case also has **Open workbench**; see [Bookkeeping workbench](/en/bookkeeping/getting-started/).

| Tab | Contents |
|---|---|
| **Timeline** | What has happened on the case. Select **Post a Note** to add a note. |
| **Tasks** | The case checklist, by section. Each task shows **Not started**, **In progress** or **Done**. Use **+ Add task** to add one, and **Assign to me** in a task's **⋯** menu to take it. A task that runs in a workflow has **Open form ↗**. |
| **Time & Budget** | The quoted fee and the invoices of the case. |
| **Documents** | The files of the case, in the folders that the workflow creates. |
| **Details** | **Basics**, **Key Dates**, the **Work team** (each role and its member, and the **Case owner**), the client and **Privacy**. |

**Who can see a case.** The **Privacy** section of **Details** says who can see the case's documents: normally the members of the case's department, the managers above the case owner, and tenant admins. If the client company is limited to an access list, only the people on that list, the case's assignee and its creator can open the documents.

## Notifications

Select **Notifications** in the side bar. Notifications are grouped by **Today**, **Yesterday**, **This week** and **Earlier**, and can be filtered with **All**, **Unread**, **Tasks**, **Approvals** and **System**. Select a notification to open what it is about — for example, the case of a task. **Mark all read** clears the unread count.

To choose which notifications also come by e-mail, see [Personal settings and help](/en/getting-started/settings-help/#your-settings).

## Team

Select **Team** in the side bar for the firm's directory: the departments on the left, and the people and AI employees of each department on the right. Use **Directory** or **Org chart** to change the view, and the search box to find a department, a person or an AI employee. **Chat** on an AI employee's card opens a chat with it.
